This repository contains framework-integration packages (for pydantic-ai,
LangChain, LiteLLM, Microsoft Agent Framework, Haystack, LlamaIndex,
Ray Serve, vLLM, the Vercel AI SDK, and n8n) that talk to a customer's own
self-hosted Algenta Engine over its public HTTP/MCP APIs at runtime — never
a bundled or local engine. It does not contain, vendor, or depend on the
Algenta Engine or its runtime, which are separately distributed and subject
to the Algenta Engine license, not Apache-2.0. A package in this repository
depends on at most one Algenta-owned library — the published `algenta-sdk`
package (PyPI and npm) — and several packages depend on no Algenta-owned
library at all. See scripts/check-no-engine-dependency.py, which is run in
CI on every pull request to enforce this boundary mechanically, not just by
policy.
